  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NWP programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NWP Programme is an umbrella program with several projects.

Project 1. Young Expert Programmes (YEP): Water &amp; Agrofood
The Young Expert Programmes Water &amp; Agrofood (YEP) offer Young Dutch and national Experts the opportunity to gain working experience in an international environment in the Water (since 2013) and Agrofood (since 2015) sectors. Through YEP, Young Experts work for one or two years at a Dutch company, knowledge institute or NGO (or their local counterparts) on topics such as Efficient Water Management, Access to Safe Drinking Water, Eradicating Hunger and Malnutrition, or Creating Sustainable Food Systems. Moreover, Young Experts gain access to a personal development programme (training and coaching) and the  Global YEP Alumni Network. As such, YEP supports the creation of a pool of international Water and Agrofood experts, helps to contribute to the achievement of the SDGs and promotes the work of Dutch Water and Agrofood organisations working aboard.</narrative>
  </description>
